      "id": "gp8rlic",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of National Income"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Gross Domestic Product (GDP) measures the total monetary value of final goods and services produced within a nation's geographical territory.",
        "Gross National Product (GNP) calculates the total value produced by normal residents, accounting for Net Factor Income from Abroad (NFIA).",
        "Net National Product (NNP) at Factor Cost is considered the official measure of National Income after accounting for depreciation.",
        "Three distinct calculation methods exist for National Income: the Value Added (Product) Method, the Income Method, and the Expenditure Method.",
        "Key limitations in estimating National Income include non-monetary transactions, the informal economy, and double counting."
      ],
      "id": "7y37f8d"
    },
